I am deeply saddened by the passing of Phumzile Mlambo Ngcuka, former Executive Director of UN Women and a remarkable leader who devoted her life to advancing women's rights and gender equality.

I remember with great fondness her visit to #Senegal in 2018, which left a lasting impression on all of us who had the privilege of welcoming her. Her warmth and genuine commitment to advancing the rights of women and girls made that visit truly memorable.

My heartfelt condolences to her family, loved ones and the entire UN Women community.
@rosensarr
@UN_Women

